-- check/bad: three values in a circle (`language.md` §7). The message walks
-- it in order — `a → b → c → a` — because a reader has to see which step is
-- the one they meant to break, and a set of three names does not say.
--
-- The declarations are written in the order the circle runs, so the anchor
-- and the source order agree here; `CyclicValueChain`'s job is the PATH.
pub a : Int
a =
    b + 1


pub b : Int
b =
    c + 1


pub c : Int
c =
    a + 1
